<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Acre</h1><p class="st-meta">1899 CE – 1903 CE · capital Puerto Alonso</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived state proclaimed by Brazilian rubber tappers in Bolivian territory, whose struggle ended with Brazil buying Acre in 1903.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> boom, thousands of Brazilian rubber tappers settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, which belonged to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Bolivia</a> by treaty. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> set up a customs post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-alonso">Puerto Alonso</a> in 1899, the Spanish adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-galvez-rodriguez-de-arias">Luis Gálvez Rodríguez de Arias</a>, backed by local interests, proclaimed the Independent State of Acre on 14 July 1899.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-galvez-rodriguez-de-arias">Gálvez</a> declared himself president and set up ministries and decrees in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-alonso">Puerto Alonso</a>, intending eventual union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, which still recognised Bolivian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, sent a force that removed him in 1900. Conflict revived in 1902 when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Bolivia</a> leased the region to an Anglo-American company, the Bolivian Syndicate, and the Brazilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/placido-de-castro">José Plácido de Castro</a> led an armed uprising of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> tappers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/placido-de-castro">Plácido de Castro</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-alonso">Puerto Alonso</a> in 1903, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a> occupied the territory. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-petropolis">Treaty of Petrópolis</a> in 1903 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Republic of Bolivia</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> for £2 million and the promise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madeira-mamore-railway">Madeira-Mamoré</a> railway.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-acre.jpg" alt="Republic of Acre" width="320" height="176"><figcaption>Image: User:Giro720 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_do_Estado_Independente_do_Acre.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1899 CE – 1903 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Puerto Alonso</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Luis Gálvez Rodríguez de Arias, Plácido de Castro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/brazil">Brazil</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Independent State of Acre, Estado Independente do Acre</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1901&amp;focus=republic-of-acre" aria-label="Republic of Acre on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2810 2550 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Acre lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3130 2806L3235 3140M3130 2806L3845 3279"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3235 3140h0M3845 3279h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3130 2806h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3130 2806h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1901&amp;focus=republic-of-acre">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
